# Persist saved Analysis items

Prevent saved production checks and plans from disappearing when Analysis is dismissed and reopened.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Saving a production check or plan writes it to persistent application/game state rather than sheet-local view state.
- [x] Saved items remain available after closing and reopening Analysis.
- [x] Saved items remain available after terminating and relaunching the application.
- [x] Saved items remain associated with their player, kind, icon, name, cards, and ordered construction steps.
- [x] Editing an existing item updates the persisted item without creating a duplicate.
- [x] Existing saved-data decoding remains backward compatible, including records without a selected icon.
- [x] Analysis items persist as part of the active game and are cleared only when a fresh game replaces it through SCR-000.
- [x] Persistence ownership avoids global mutable state and preserves serializability.
- [x] Domain regression coverage verifies save, sheet reload, app relaunch reload, edit, player isolation, kind isolation, and fresh-game clearing.
- [x] App, unit-test, and UI-test bundles compile.
- [ ] Focused persistence checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Scope notes

- This is the critical REQ-017 defect and should be completed before the remaining REQ-017 presentation tasks.
- TASK-040 owns the burger menu and New Game navigation; this task supplies the active-game persistence boundary it consumes.
- Do not implement simulation storage or a multi-game document browser unless separately required.

## Evidence

- Moved custom Analysis items into the serializable `BoardSnapshot` active-game state with backward-compatible empty decoding.
- Added identity-based save/update behavior on `BoardState` and removed sheet-local plan ownership.
- Added `ActiveGamePersistence` with injected `UserDefaults` coverage for full snapshot save, reload, and clearing.
- UI coverage closes and reopens Analysis after saving and verifies the item remains visible.
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing` compiled the app, unit tests, and UI tests successfully.
